print("DEMO: compare live Agentrail help with the frozen training interface");
print("Scenario: Agentrail may evolve after an adapter is trained. Capture its current command and option interface only at evaluation time; classify every command as trained, rejected out of scope, or unsupported by the frozen contract.");
print("Native boundary: the shell captures bounded top-level and per-command help and extracts option names; MLPL enforces budgets and deterministically checks next, begin, and complete signatures. No model decides drift.");
print("Budgets: 16384 top-level help bytes, 16384 bytes per subcommand, 131072 option-manifest bytes, 1024 version bytes, at most 64 live commands, three frozen trained commands, zero training writes.");
print("Deterministic comparison:");
print(r);
print("Interpretation: trained_commands are the three frozen workflow actions with intact option signatures; rejected_out_of_scope counts live commands the adapter was never taught; unsupported_trained_contracts counts missing commands or changed required options. Live help remains evaluation evidence only.");
ok(1)
